# Example only, NOT sops-encrypted -- this repo's own .sops.yaml carries a
# placeholder recipient nobody holds the private half of, so nothing here
# could be decrypted even if it were real ciphertext. Real secrets belong in
# your own private config repo, encrypted with your own age key; see
# docs/bootstrap.md's sops section.
#
# Key names are whatever you list in user.nix's `secrets` field -- sops-nix
# doesn't care what they're called, and this framework has no opinion on
# what secrets you need. The two below are illustrative only.
#
# To create the real file: `age-keygen` for a keypair, put your public key
# in your own private repo's .sops.yaml, then `sops secrets.yaml` in that
# repo to open $EDITOR on a new encrypted file.
GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN: "example-placeholder-value"
MY_SERVICE_PAT: "example-placeholder-value"
